{"diagnosis": "Trace shows tohost FAIL 0xdead with TRAP: fetch misalign addr low bits nonzero instead of aligned fetch progress. Expected mem_la_addr[1:0]==2'b00 but excerpt drives 2'b10. Root cause is picorv32.v:382 where mem_la_addr forces low bits to 2'b10 for both fetch/prefetch and data paths, making every lookahead access misaligned.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -382,1 +382,1 @@
-	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b10} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b10};
+	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b00} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b00};", "expected": "tohost PASS with no TRAP: fetch misalign addr low bits nonzero, VERDICT pass:true (checksum != a29998cd8e81501b64b44a66e009c12b297662db5ef5369b12ef3feae608e5d5)"}

